{"version":2,"width":100,"height":39,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"title":"agk run --namespace: demo/pi"}
[0.001753, "o", "\u001b[1;34mpi\u001b[0m \u001b[2m$\u001b[0m cat agentiik.yaml\r\n"]
[1.00429, "o", "apiVersion: agentiik.dev/v1\r\nkind: Workflow\r\nmetadata: { name: pi, namespace: demo }\r\ninputs:\r\n  darts: { schema: { type: integer, minimum: 1 }, default: 100000 }\r\noutputs:\r\n  estimates: { from: { step: throw, port: out } }\r\n  pi: { from: { step: average, port: out } }\r\nsteps:\r\n  players:\r\n    image: alpine:3.21\r\n    script:\r\n      - printf '{\"player\":\"%s\"}\\n' ada grace linus alan | /agk/bin/agk emit out\r\n    outputs: [out]\r\n  throw:\r\n    image: python:3.13-alpine\r\n    needs: [{ step: players, port: out, as: in }]\r\n    strategy: { fan_out: item }\r\n    params: { player: \"${{ item.data.player }}\", darts: \"${{ workflow.inputs.darts }}\" }\r\n    shell: [python3]\r\n    script:\r\n      - import os, random, sys\r\n      - player, darts = os.environ[\"AGK_PARAM_PLAYER\"], int(os.environ[\"AGK_PARAM_DARTS\"])\r\n      - random.seed(player)\r\n      - pi = 4 * sum(random.random() ** 2 + random.random() ** 2 < 1 for _ in range(darts)) / darts\r\n      - print(f\"{player} threw {darts} darts, pi is about {pi}\", file=sys.stderr)\r\n      - print(f\"{player} threw {darts} darts, pi is about {pi}\")\r\n    outputs: [out]\r\n  average:\r\n    image: python:3.13-alpine\r\n    needs: [{ step: throw, port: out, as: in }]\r\n    shell: [python3]\r\n    script:\r\n      - import json, sys\r\n      - pis = [float(i[\"data\"][\"stdout\"].split()[-1]) for i in json.load(sys.stdin)[\"items\"]]\r\n      - print(sum(pis) / len(pis))\r\n    outputs: [out]\r\n"]
[4.005574, "o", "\u001b[1;34mpi\u001b[0m \u001b[2m$\u001b[0m agk push --namespace demo\r\n"]
[5.033727, "o", "user namespace remapping is off on this daemon and this runner does not require it, so the floor is lifted: a task's files are owned by a real uid on the host, root inside a container is the host's own root, and a process that escapes a container is that account rather than an unprivileged high-numbered one that maps to no real user.\r\n"]
[5.411056, "o", "python:3.13-alpine resolved to python@sha256:79e7a9b9ff1cbceff819f856fb374477792a5967759d94df266de7b7b4120e6f\r\n"]
[5.75592, "o", "alpine:3.21 resolved to alpine@sha256:ce64758a109eb420d874a118f87920e625e12d3634e03b4a5573fd9f6e5d3507\r\n"]
